  stan4bart-wide-prior-followups: two follow-ups of the wide-prior fix
    on stan4bart main. (1) The Newton solve for a Student-t or Cauchy
    coordinate's origin has no guard on its slope where the degrees of
    freedom are below 0.4, below which the transform is no longer
    increasing; guard it (a nit of the review, the solve converging in
    at most 9 steps on every finite input tried). (2) normal(500, 2.5)
    has a coordinate scale equal to the prior's, so the fix leaves it
    as before, and it mixes worse than 0.0-13 did; the fix cannot
    change it without moving the draws of narrow priors. Ruled
    (dec-B788): the follow-up is not bound to bit-identity of the fits
    the fix leaves alone; it may move narrow-prior and, if it pays,
    default fits where a comparison against 0.0-13 shows better mixing
    at equal time, judged by interval coverage. Found at the same
    sitting (C82): normal(500, 2.5) leaves both chains near 500 where
    the posterior is near 2.1, on main and on 0.0-13 alike, so it is a
    sampler failure and not slow mixing; the NEWS claim for far-
    centered priors was corrected. Not built.
