  one-thread-mechanism: (dec-B765, Q4 of the C++ quality review) one
    runOnWorkers(n, body) keeping the first exception at the three
    sampler sites (run, grow-from-root, predict) and a persistent C++
    pool owned by the chain for test-row routing; delete the C thread
    manager (571 lines) and its configure probes, about 570 lines out
    and 120 in. Gated on a same-machine timing on the bench machine,
    interleaved A/B at and around the routing cutoff, before the
    build; if the pool is slower there, take the alternative: keep the
    C manager, fix its inverted cleanup flags and unify the three C++
    sites (about 60 lines). Not built.
  state-forest-reader: (dec-B766, Q5 of the C++ quality review) merge
    the restore and warm-start readers of a saved state into one that
    fills a per-forest record the variance forest's ten slots fill
    too, with no static error buffer, about 150 lines, and add a kind
    field on the state's forest list entries if they do not already
    record their kind, before the 1.0 format freezes. Moving the
    variance forest to a list entry later stays possible: a writer
    change plus one old-format conversion branch. Not built.
  family-fact-records: (dec-B767, Q3 of the C++ quality review) one
    constant record per kind of response (8 kinds, Student-t its own
    row, multinomial a row), beside its code, in a table that fails
    the build if a kind lacks a record, read by the engine, the bridge
    and the factories in place of family-name tests; behavior stays
    virtual, and each move keeps one eligibility predicate evaluated
    per sweep. Anchor and basis-scale expressions move verbatim: the
    record stores inputs or a flag, never a precomputed constant. A
    tests/cpp check that each class's virtual answers match its row.
    About 400 lines with tests, 8 to 12 agent-hours. After the
    collapsed-move rebuild lands and before the C creation entry and
    facts struct; planned together with sampler-core-and-capabilities
    under a blind critique; engine review with a same-machine timing
    before and after. Not built.
  latent-freshness-rule: (from the Q3 reviews, agent call) a step that
    moves a row's conditional between latent draws owes that row an
    exact fresh draw before anything reads its latent; this
    generalizes the marked-row rule to in-sweep moves. Amend the
    approximate-draws plan (its S2 carries it) and note it in the
    k-move-pricing plan. Source: scratch/famtraits/mcmc.md and the
    synthesis's section (iii).
    Deferred (Q3 follow-on ii-3): how the collapsed move meets the
    approximate route, decline where any row would take it or mark
    every row, comes to the maintainer beside dec-B623's look at
    k-move step 2's timings, when approximate-draws S2 is planned;
    neither branch is on main, and declining narrows dec-B619. Not built.

absolute residual prior scale (decided, VD 2026-09-14)
  post-release, R only: chisq gains an absolute spelling,
  chisq(df, scale = lambda), which names the prior literally instead of
  through the sigest its quantile calibrates against, and ignores
  sigest as fixed() does. Additive - a new argument beside quant, no
  spelling retired, so no tombstone. The residual prior's one home on
  the family object is the surface it is added to (docs/decisions.md
  dec-B123). scheduled after 1.0-0 (VD 2026-09-14).

